Z||000000||2FAST4U||01-12-2000||09:24 PM||||Lately there has been a lot of negative comments on this forum about buying and selling parts.<BR>I would like to take this time to recognize a couple of forum members for exceptional business practices.<BR>Today I recieved a large shipment from FieroDave. It was packeged to withstand any shipping abuses. It arrived even sooner than expected. The package even included some attached hardware and wiring that I didn't pay for. JOB WELL DONE!<BR>I also ordered some stuff from SuperXmotorsports and sent a money order for more than I should have. SuperX let me know of the mistake immeadiatly to return the difference. He even saved the items for a couple of weeks while I put together enough money. Thanks Much.<BR>I also won an ebay auction on some parts from Mrfiero, simce we live in the same city he delivered the stuff to my house te very next day. Thats Service.<BR>I recommend any of these guys for service beyond the call of duty.<BR>So far I have never had a bad experience buying from other forum members.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 2FAST4U (edited 01-12-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||fiero56||01-12-2000||10:36 PM||||Somebody, I don't even know their Forum name, is sending me an ash tray light socket for nothing. They even took care of shipping! I haven't had any bad experiences yet either, but I haven't bought a very much yet.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||01-12-2000||10:46 PM||||I've found that members of this forum are some of the nicest people you would ever want to do business with.  I've sold/bought/sent/given away stuff to some members and been very satisfied.  I've received some things, too (some where even free!).  Always a friendly attitude, etc.  There's even one member that is holding some parts for me (with a very small deposit) until I can come up with the money.  How many other (non-forum) members would do that?  My guess would be...none!||||reg||1
Z||000003||SloPonti||01-13-2000||12:20 AM||||i reccommend fierodave!! i think very highly of him! i have never met him but we have done buisness with some parts several time! he is currently helping me with making me a website for my new motor on his site! fierodave is a great guy! i have bought and sold on the internet for a long time now and i think by fat he is the best i have worked with! in the long time i have been buying and selling i have come across some problems with some people though-like no sending money or not sending parts! i really hate that! think if you want it then send the money and if someone sent you money then do the right thing and send the part!<BR>thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||01-13-2000||12:28 AM||||I will have to give another thumbs up to TOM and also FieroDave. Even when Tom could have sold me parts (that I probably didn't really need) he emailed me about other less costly alternatives. He could have very easily made several dollars from me on this sale, but tried to save me money instead! FieroDave sent me a set of heads with the manifolds still attached along with rockers, tach filter and brackets attached for an awesome price. Both have treated me very well and I will look forward to more business with both of them.||||reg||1
Z||000005||AL||01-13-2000||01:38 AM||||i second that, fiero dave is tops, sold me a fiero bra with the logo on it, and i know he sent it before he got my money order, it arrived a day before christmas and my car looks great with this bra, i know i will keep in touch with dave.||||reg||14
Z||000006||DXR_DAD||01-13-2000||09:16 PM||||THIS IS A PLUG!! I have ordered form Tom and I just want to say that it always feels good to know that he has what you want. He is very easy to get to. He e-mails you as soon as you send your e-mail and the parts are in good shape and shipped on time.<P>Thanks Tom for helping us FieroNs!!!<P><BR>I just got a shipment from SuperX today, man that was fast!!! I e-mailed him, he e-mailed with a pic....bingo.... done deal.....sold....It was nice to do business with him.  Thanks SuperX, It's at the paint shop. <P>||||reg||14
Z||000007||Bruce||01-13-2000||09:44 PM||||I've also dealt with TOM, and he always let's me know exactly the status of a delivery, and produces great products.<BR>George, at The Fiero Shop, could have soaked me for a pedal replacement, but promptly gave me the right explanation for my problem. I know that any other mechanic would have gladly done the work, taken my money, and not thought twice about it. I'm going to the Fiero Shop for any subsequent mechanical work!<BR>And, thanks to all you guys for all the help and suggestions since I joined the forum.||||reg||1
Z||000008||BlackGT||01-14-2000||03:46 AM||||I have not done any business with any members of this forum but I have joined a club here in Atlanta called the Georgia Fieros. What a nice group of people!! One of the members I call on a regular basis since he has a ton of <BR>info as well as parts for any part of the Fiero (all years) I`ve been living in Atlanta<BR>for a year and a half (origionally from NYC)<BR>and have come to realize that most people are<BR>generally honest and if you share a common interest would bend over backwards for you<BR>to enjoy their love of the interest as well.<BR>When I see other Fiero owners on the street<BR>I wave and when someone asks me about my<BR>car I am more than willing to share what I know or even pointing them in the right direction.....after all isn`t that what it`s all about!!!!||||reg||6
